WEBVTT

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.060
<i>Dear Grandmother,</i>

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:09.720
<i>I had a wonderful time composing 
a song with QUARTET NIGHT.</i>

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:17.760
<i>A lot happened, but we managed to write 
a great song for the Triple S entry concert.</i>

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.000
<i>STARISH is progressing by leaps and bounds. </i>

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.410
<i>Through their cross-unit project, their unique members</i>

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.000
<i>are shining brighter than ever.</i>

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:35.000
<i>Will STARISH appear at the Triple S entry concert?</i>

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.030
<i>I'm sure they will.</i>

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:38.610
<i>There's no way they won't.</i>

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.640
<i>QUARTET NIGHT and STARISH are the best.</i>

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.690
The deadline is nearly here.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:54.120
Are you really not going to enter STARISH?

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.230
Look at this.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.160
People are expecting 
more and more from STARISH.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:09.180
Do you have any idea what effect 
not entering STARISH will have?

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.540
What will you do, Shiny?

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.770
Our shoot starts at 1:00 PM, right?

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.630
Yes.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:27.540
Let's go over the show before rehearsal.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:30.980
Rei-chan.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.440
You're back from your trip.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:37.980
Haruka?

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.090
Haruka isn't with you?

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:48.930
What?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.590
Um...

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.880
She's not coming back.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.080
What?

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.400
She's not coming back?

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.770
Uh? What?

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:06.470
What do you mean?

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:10.200
You haven't been entered yet, have you?

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:16.230
You won't be performing with us after all.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:20.400
But we haven't given up.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.900
We'll be at the entry concert.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.020
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.450
What is this?

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.900
Our entry song.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.170
We wrote it with her.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:38.630
It's the greatest song.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.460
The greatest song...

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.380
She's the one who said 
she didn't want to come back.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.080
No...

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.370
Why?

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.350
You don't know?

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:56.900
If you don't, we might 
have to take her from you.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.700
Because of Love

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.660
This one.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:17.620
It's QUARTET NIGHT's entry song 
that arrived this morning.

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.400
I've already listened to it.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:27.380
Go ahead. Give it a listen.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:24.530
That's QUARTET NIGHT's Triple S entry song.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:25.940
It's amazing.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.730
The music was practically glowing.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:35.410
Their appeal came together 
to create an unprecedented harmony.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:39.710
This is the song the little lamb wrote.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:41.670
It's perfect.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:46.060
Everyone would deem it 
worthy of a Triple S entry.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:52.090
I had no idea Haruka had this side to her.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:58.580
Do you think the fact 
we haven't entered the Triple S

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:03.120
is related to Haruka's refusal to return?

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.610
Of course not.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:10.110
Haru-chan believed more than 
anyone that we'd be entered.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:14.430
Don't worry. She'll be back soon.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.200
You're right.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.400
Let's focus on the work before us.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:23.500
We have to keep moving forward.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:24.840
Yeah.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:26.420
You're right.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.880
Yep.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:32.230
We should focusing on doing what we can.

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:35.350
You're right. I'll do my best.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:40.570
STARISH, get ready.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.110
Thank you for waiting.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:49.420
Here's STARISH!

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:55.520
You're as popular as ever.

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.080
Thank you.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.290
Your cross-unit project was a huge success.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:03.670
That rock musical must have been tough.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:04.980
Yeah.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:06.960
At first, we had no idea what to do.

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:11.350
Both Otoya-kun and I were at a loss.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.100
But we tried a lot of different things.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:19.930
Thanks to everyone's support, 
we enjoyed performing onstage.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:24.850
We sang the theme song of a new smart phone.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:27.950
We had to suggest a concept 
for the commercial.

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:31.160
That was really hard.

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:35.170
Our disagreements turned into arguments.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:37.830
You two were so stubborn.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.730
You're one to talk.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:43.540
The other members were 
really worried about us.

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:49.770
But because we took the job so seriously, 
we were satisfied with the results.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:53.260
Tokiya and Hijirikawa had a tough time, too.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:58.120
We lost sight of the big picture 
because of the pressure.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:04.390
But we were able to enjoy the music festival 
because of the support from our friends.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.730
The cross-unit experience

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:13.130
gave us confidence and taught us 
the importance of friendship.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:19.070
We only finished the job because 
we had faith in each other.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:24.060
We're also grateful 
to the staff we worked with.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:30.520
And more than anything, the fans 
are looking forward to our performances.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.250
Also...

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:45.520
So STARISH hopes you'll keep on...

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.100
...believing in us.

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:58.070
It's strange.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.130
I feel like our hearts are finally one.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:07.040
You're wrong. We've always been one.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:12.370
Haruka brought us together.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:21.720
She's only been away for a day, 
but I miss her already.

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:25.650
I want to see her more than ever.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:27.230
Me, too.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.180
You know...

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:42.370
Nanami's always been a hard worker.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:43.500
Yes.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:51.880
She inspires those around her 
to want to work hard, too.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:58.560
Once she gathered 
the lyrics somebody tore up.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:01.320
That's our cherished memory.

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:10.270
She's exceptionally clumsy, 
but also exceptionally pure.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:18.780
That's why being with her feels so comfortable.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:27.290
Before I knew it, being away 
from her became unthinkable.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:36.090
After meeting Haruka, 
I learned the importance of friends.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:46.350
All because of her and the songs she writes.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:04.700
Let's definitely perform 
at the Triple S entry concert.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:09.950
We will show Nanami the Triple S 
opening ceremony's stage.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:13.000
We won't let QUARTET NIGHT take Nanami.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:17.090
With her song, we'll stand 
on the entry concert's stage.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.300
Yes, definitely.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:23.010
We can fly because she believes in us.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:29.380
Her songs will take us 
to even greater heights.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.440
Let's go...

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:44.150
...to see Nanami.

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:26.740
Nanami.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:30.550
Welcome back.

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:32.300
Welcome back.

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:33.890
Welcome back.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.390
Welcome back.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.270
Welcome back.

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:38.770
Welcome back.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.650
Welcome back, Haruka.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:09.390
Nanami.

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:10.260
Haru-chan.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:11.120
Nanami.

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:12.040
Milady.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:12.890
Nanami.

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:13.940
Nanami-san.

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:14.700
Haruka.

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:18.410
Write a song with us.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.660
Write a song with us.

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:22.910
Write a song with us.

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:25.170
Write a song with us.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:27.420
Write a song with us.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:30.130
Write a song with us.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:32.630
Write a song with us.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:40.690
We want to perform 
at the Triple S entry concert.

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:45.130
We must perform one of your songs.

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:46.600
Please, Haruka.

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:50.280
Write us a Triple S entry song.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:17:00.810
I actually wrote 
a Triple S entry song for you.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:03.850
What?

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:06.810
You did?

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.880
Really, Haruka?

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.160
Yes.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:13.210
I...

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:33.610
<i>I felt compelled to write your song.</i>

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.630
This is our Triple S entry song.

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:41.330
Incredible. This is amazing, Nanami.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.410
Fantastic.

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:45.690
This is the best, milady.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.160
It's perfect.

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.050
Way to go, Haru-chan.

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:54.090
This song is packed full of our goddess's love.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:55.620
Guys...

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.330
It's really amazing.

00:17:58.330 --> 00:18:01.430
I want to sing this song right now.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:07.140
Let's write some lyrics immediately.

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:09.770
What? Right now?

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:11.560
Of course.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.440
Strike while the iron is hot.

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:15.940
Will you help us, milady?

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:21.700
Of course. Let me help you shine.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.030
All right!

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:25.650
Thank you, Haru-chan.

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:27.910
For writing us a song.

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:16.790
How long are you going to—

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:57.450
Sheesh.

00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:00.540
How long are you going to sleep?

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:01.970
Wake up!

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:06.800
What's going on?

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.370
I'm tired.

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:14.510
Good morning.

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:15.470
Morning.

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:16.770
You scared me.

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:18.580
It's already morning.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:19.960
Seems that way.

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:22.410
The night passed by so quickly.

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:42.580
Hurry. You'll be late for work.

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:46.280
Uh, oh!

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:47.360
Let's hurry.

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:49.110
Wait!

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:50.660
Wait up!

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:09.080
You were serious, weren't you?

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:09.730
What?

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:13.440
About taking Haruka from them.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:16.730
Of course.

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:18.710
I'm always serious.

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:22.330
I'm jealous.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:24.880
No one asked her to do it.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:28.870
But she believed in them 
and wrote them a song.

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:39.730
This is...

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:46.400
Because of Love

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:58.420
Did you listen to our song?

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:06.590
Please let us enter the Triple S.

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:29.070
Your revolution is not yet complete!

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:09.730
How's your revolution coming along?

00:24:09.730 --> 00:24:10.630
Uta Pri!
